# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Prettier is configured `endOfLine: "lf"`. Without this file, a Windows clone
# with `core.autocrlf=true` checks every file out as CRLF, and `pnpm
# format:check` then fails on hundreds of files whose content is byte-identical
# apart from the line terminator — while the same check passes in CI on Linux.
# That is a confusing failure to hand a new contributor, and it recurs on every
# merge that touches a lot of files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from language statistics, but still
# reviewable when you ask for it.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
